node_modules/
.bundlebox/var/
.bundlebox/out/
*.log
*.tgz
.DS_Store
kernel/target/
expert/**/__pycache__/

# A workspace's own corpora, world models and service list are INPUTS, not
# derived artefacts, so they are meant to be committed in the repo they describe.
# This repo is the tool AND one workspace: the `bb` corpus describes bundlebox
# itself and CI runs it, so it is committed and the exceptions below say exactly
# which paths that covers. Everything else under .bundlebox/ here is a fixture
# from developing on one machine and committing it would ship local state as if
# it were part of the package.
#
# git cannot re-include a path inside an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY, so these exclude
# the directory's contents (`dir/*`) rather than the directory itself. Written
# as `dir/` the negations below are silently dead and the corpus never ships.
.bundlebox/cookbook/*
!.bundlebox/cookbook/bb/
.bundlebox/genesis/*
!.bundlebox/genesis/bb/
!.bundlebox/genesis/current.json
.bundlebox/runbook/*
!.bundlebox/runbook/services.json
.bundlebox/simulate/
.bundlebox/frames/
.bundlebox/failsafe/
.bundlebox/blackice/
# Derived from whatever `bb scan` found on THIS machine this week, so it is a
# local artefact even though the verb that reads it is not. `bb bench init`
# rebuilds it anywhere in under a second.
.bundlebox/bench/

# The auditor keeps two kinds of artefact side by side and they have opposite
# rules. A CHARTER is derived from the tree and is re-derived when the tree
# moves, so it is regenerable and does not belong in git — committing one means
# reviewing a diff nobody wrote. A REVIEW is a dated record a person or a model
# produced, it is never edited, and its whole value is being a fixed point to
# measure drift against, so it is committed.
.bundlebox/auditor/*/charter.json
.bundlebox/auditor/*/charter.md

# Claude Code keeps two settings files side by side and they have opposite
# rules. `settings.json` is the PROJECT's: `bb wire` writes the hook rows there
# and every contributor should get the same ones, so it is committed.
# `settings.local.json` is one person's permission allowlist for their own box —
# committing it hands everyone else's agent a set of approvals they never gave.
.claude/settings.local.json
